    contentHtml: `<h2>Source / episode metadata</h2>
<ul> <li>The accessible episode listing is titled <strong>“International Market Volatility, Anthropic’s Debut, and Gemini Catches Up | #314”</strong>. The page exposed only a relative timestamp (“yesterday 02:10:45”), not an exact calendar publication date in the captured text. <span>[page1visit3]</span></li> <li>The related BigGo news companion piece is titled <strong>“Steve Jurvetson says SpaceX's real bet isn't rockets , it’s compute at 60% of industry cost.”</strong> <span>[page97visit2]</span></li>
</ul> <h2>Gemini 4 Neon: launch, pricing, availability</h2>
<ul> <li><strong>Launch date:</strong> November 18, 2026. <span>[page2visit2]</span> <span>[page17visit2]</span></li> <li><strong>Pricing:</strong> $3 per million input tokens and $15 per million output tokens; cached input tokens are $0.15 per million, reflecting a 95% discount. <span>[page2visit2]</span> <span>[page17visit2]</span></li> <li><strong>Context window:</strong> 1 million tokens. <span>[page2visit2]</span> <span>[page17visit2]</span></li> <li><strong>Availability:</strong> rolling out via the Gemini API / Google AI Studio, Gemini for business / enterprise surfaces, Google Antigravity for paid Pro and Ultra users, and the Gemini app for Pro and Ultra subscribers. <span>[page2visit2]</span> <span>[page17visit2]</span></li>
</ul> <h2>Gemini 4 Neon: independent benchmark results and limits</h2>
<ul> <li><strong>Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index:</strong> 61 at xhigh; 60 at high; 55 at medium; 44 at low. It ranks <strong>#3 overall</strong>, behind GPT-6.2 Astra (max) and Claude Fable 5.2 (max). <span>[page9websearch2]</span> <span>[page17websearch3]</span></li> <li><strong>Cost / speed on that index:</strong> about <strong>$6.44 per task</strong> at xhigh, about 17% less than Gemini 4 Carbon’s $7.76 at standard pricing, and about <strong>21 minutes per task</strong> versus Carbon’s roughly 36 minutes. <span>[page17websearch3]</span></li> <li><strong>Other independent outcomes cited by Google / Artificial Analysis:</strong> #2 on the Vals Index (70.9%); #1 on the Legal Research Bench and Tax Agent Bench; #1 on the Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index (58.6); #1 on Terminal-Bench Science (70.5%), RiemannBench (84.0%), and HLE-Diamond (71.3%); plus strong results on Chartography, Agents’ Last Exam, AutomationBench, and Vending-Bench 2. <span>[page2visit2]</span> <span>[page17visit2]</span></li> <li><strong>Limits / caveats:</strong> Neon is presented as a paid-tier model with a 1M-token context window, four effort levels (low, medium, high, xhigh), and text/image/video/speech input with text output. Google’s safety note also says some cyber access is limited to the Fairwind Program / trusted defenders. <span>[page2visit2]</span> <span>[page3websearch2]</span></li>
</ul> <h2>Anthropic IPO: official pricing, trading dates, and totals</h2>
<ul> <li><strong>Official IPO price:</strong> $83.00 per share. <span>[page62websearch1]</span> <span>[page62visit2]</span></li> <li><strong>Trading began:</strong> November 19, 2026 on Nasdaq under ticker <strong>ANT</strong>. <span>[page62websearch1]</span> <span>[page63visit2]</span></li> <li><strong>Expected close date announced in the offering:</strong> November 20, 2026. <span>[page62websearch1]</span></li> <li><strong>Final IPO closing totals:</strong> Anthropic announced the closing of an aggregate <strong>1,127,000,000 shares</strong> sold at $83.00, including the full exercise of the underwriters’ 147,000,000-share option. Aggregate gross proceeds were about <strong>$93.5 billion</strong>, of which about <strong>$91.6 billion</strong> was received by Anthropic. <span>[page63visit2]</span></li> <li><strong>Concurrent private placement:</strong> Anthropic also closed the sale of <strong>313,253,007 Class N shares</strong> to AMD, Broadcom, Google, Micron, Microsoft, Nvidia, and TSMC Partners for about <strong>$26.0 billion</strong>. Combined gross proceeds were about <strong>$119.5 billion</strong>. <span>[page63visit2]</span></li>
</ul> <h2>Anthropic share move on Nov. 20 and the market catalyst</h2>
<ul> <li><strong>Final Nov. 20 close:</strong> Anthropic closed at <strong>$88.91</strong>, down <strong>8.5%</strong> from the prior close. <span>[page43websearch1]</span> <span>[page85visit2]</span></li> <li><strong>Context:</strong> Reuters said the Nasdaq fell <strong>5.3%</strong> that day, the S&amp;P 500 fell <strong>3.7%</strong>, and the VIX jumped to 37. Anthropic’s decline came amid a broader AI / tech selloff. <span>[page85visit2]</span></li> <li><strong>Broad catalyst:</strong> the selloff was tied to Nvidia’s <strong>14% drop</strong> after Reuters reported the SEC was probing its accounting, along with worries about AI spending not generating returns fast enough, rising rates, slower data-center buildouts, and general profit-taking in tech. <span>[page43visit2]</span> <span>[page85visit2]</span> <span>[page47visit2]</span></li>
</ul> <h2>Bottom line</h2>
<ul> <li><strong>Gemini 4 Neon</strong> launched on Nov. 18, 2026 at $3/$15 per 1M tokens, with a 1M-token context window and broad paid availability.</li> <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> priced its IPO at $83, began trading Nov. 19, and closed the offering Nov. 20 with $93.5B in gross IPO proceeds before adding the concurrent $26B private placement.</li> <li><strong>On Nov. 20, Anthropic fell 8.5% to $88.91</strong>, in step with a broad tech rout led by Nvidia and renewed concerns about AI spending, rates, and valuation. <span>[page43websearch1]</span> <span>[page85visit2]</span></li>
</ul>`,
